================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

The MIT license above covers this project's own source code. The repository also
bundles unmodified third-party tools under tools/vendor/ so the USB flasher
(tools/flasher.py) runs with only Python 3 installed. These retain their own
licenses and copyrights, and are not covered by the MIT license above:

  esptool     4.5.1   GPL-2.0        tools/vendor/licenses/esptool-LICENSE-GPLv2.txt
  pyserial    3.5     BSD-3-Clause   tools/vendor/licenses/pyserial-LICENSE.txt
  reedsolo    1.6.0   Public domain  tools/vendor/licenses/reedsolo-LICENSE.txt

esptool is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2. It is
included and invoked as a standalone program (tools/flasher.py runs it as a
subprocess and does not import or link against it); this is mere aggregation and
does not place this project's own MIT-licensed code under the GPL. See
tools/vendor/README.md for what is bundled and how to refresh it.

Additional third-party code pulled in at build time (ESP-IDF, managed components
under managed_components/, and lib/) is governed by its own respective licenses.
